{"title":"Stinner Launches Stoic Components with Three Carbon Wheelsets, Plus a Select 2.0 Refresh","link":"https://bikerumor.com/stinner-launches-stoic-components-with-three-carbon-wheelsets-plus-a-select-2-0-refresh/","date":1795101680000,"content":"<p><img src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-hero-e1795027994840.jpeg\" width=\"1180\" height=\"660\" alt=\"(Photos / Stinner Frameworks)\" /></p>\n<p>Stinner Frameworks just dumped a pretty big fall/winter update on us. It includes a reworked Select lineup, a brand-new in-house component brand, and a titanium photo stick. It’s a lot of news for one press release, so let’s get into it.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-first-pic.jpeg\"><img width=\"1000\" height=\"667\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-first-pic.jpeg\" alt=\"Stinner Frameworks Fall:Winter Launch first pic\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-first-pic.jpeg 1000w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-first-pic-297x198.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-first-pic-120x80.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-first-pic-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-first-pic-800x533.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-first-pic-720x480.jpeg 720w\" /></a><figcaption>The Fall/Winter launch! (Photos / Stinner Frameworks)</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2>Meet Stoic Components</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>We first got a glimpse of Stinner’s Stoic Components on the debut of the <a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/stinner-enters-the-full-suspension-world-with-the-new-romero/\" target=\"_blank\">Romero at Sea Otter</a>. Stinner’s house-brand component line comes to market with three carbon wheelsets: the R40 (all-road), G29 (gravel), and M34 (mountain/adventure).</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-hub-close.jpeg\"><img width=\"1280\" height=\"854\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-hub-close.jpeg\" alt=\"Stinner Frameworks Fall/Winter Launch hub close\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-hub-close.jpeg 1280w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-hub-close-297x198.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-hub-close-120x80.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-hub-close-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-hub-close-800x533.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-hub-close-720x480.jpeg 720w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Each wheelset starts at $1,499, and you can buy them standalone or spec them on any Stinner build. Stinner staff and ambassadors have apparently been riding prototypes for years, so this isn’t a “slap a logo on it and ship it” situation.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-hub.jpeg\"><img width=\"1280\" height=\"854\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-hub.jpeg\" alt=\"Stinner Frameworks Fall:Winter Launch hub\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-hub.jpeg 1280w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-hub-297x198.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-hub-120x80.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-hub-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-hub-800x533.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-hub-720x480.jpeg 720w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>The story behind it is worth a moment. Stoic started nearly a decade ago as a partnership with Jones Wheels, and the brand honors the memory of John Jones.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Founder Aaron Stinner put it this way: “<em>John and I planned to start a component brand together. We lost him to cancer in 2021, before we got the chance. Stoic Components is that brand. We’re starting where he would have: carbon wheels, each matched to a Stinner frame and laced to Stoic hubs. Built to stay true</em>.”</p>\n\n\n\n<p>That’s a fitting way to launch a wheel brand, and the “built to stay true” line works on more than one level. Nice. </p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Select 2.0 Upgrades</h2>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-frameset-e1795026480732.jpeg\"><img width=\"1278\" height=\"650\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-frameset-e1795026480732.jpeg\" alt=\"Stinner Frameworks Fall:Winter Launch frameset\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-frameset-e1795026480732.jpeg 1278w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-frameset-e1795026480732-297x151.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-frameset-e1795026480732-120x61.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-frameset-e1795026480732-768x391.jpeg 768w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Ok, back to the bikes. Every drop bar Select now gets built using Columbus Life tubing. In comparison to the Zona tubes that were formerly used, Columbus Life uses higher-strength Omnicrom alloy for lighter, stiffer, oversized tubes across road, gravel, and MTB builds.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-select-complete-e1795026840285.jpeg\"><img width=\"1278\" height=\"672\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-select-complete-e1795026840285.jpeg\" alt=\"Stinner Frameworks Fall:Winter Launch select complete\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-select-complete-e1795026840285.jpeg 1278w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-select-complete-e1795026840285-297x156.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-select-complete-e1795026840285-120x63.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-select-complete-e1795026840285-768x404.jpeg 768w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>They will also get SRAM Rival AXS. So, drivetrain options now include Force XPLR or a Force/XO Mullet setup. You can also add the new Stoic carbon wheels, and there are new build options from Vision and Terravail. </p>\n\n\n\n<figure>\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-select-drivetrain.jpeg\"><img width=\"1280\" height=\"854\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-select-drivetrain.jpeg\" alt=\"Stinner Frameworks Fall:Winter Launch select drivetrain\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-select-drivetrain.jpeg 1280w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-select-drivetrain-297x198.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-select-drivetrain-120x80.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-select-drivetrain-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-select-drivetrain-800x533.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-select-drivetrain-720x480.jpeg 720w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-select-bars.jpeg\"><img width=\"1280\" height=\"854\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-select-bars.jpeg\" alt=\"Stinner Frameworks Fall:Winter Launch select bars\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-select-bars.jpeg 1280w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-select-bars-297x198.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-select-bars-120x80.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-select-bars-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-select-bars-800x533.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-select-bars-720x480.jpeg 720w\" /></a></figure>\n</figure>\n\n\n\n<h3>Select 2.0 Details</h3>\n\n\n\n<ul>\n<li>Columbus Life tubing on all drop bar Select models</li>\n\n\n\n<li>SRAM Rival AXS standard on all drop bar Selects</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Optional Force XPLR or Force/XO Mullet drivetrains</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Stoic carbon wheel upgrade available</li>\n\n\n\n<li>New build options from Vision and Terravail</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2>Photo Stick 2.0</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Retail: $110</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Finally, there’s the Stinner x MADE Photo Stick 2.0, because bikes are beautiful and should be photographed. It’s fabricated in-house from Grade 9 titanium at Stinner’s Santa Barbara factory, and the big change is a new 3D-printed yoke. </p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-photos-stick-logo.jpeg\"><img width=\"1280\" height=\"854\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-photos-stick-logo.jpeg\" alt=\"Stinner Frameworks Fall:Winter Launch photos stick logo\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-photos-stick-logo.jpeg 1280w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-photos-stick-logo-297x198.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-photos-stick-logo-120x80.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-photos-stick-logo-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-photos-stick-logo-800x533.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-photos-stick-logo-720x480.jpeg 720w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul>\n<li>Grade 9 titanium, bead-blasted finish with black Stinner x MADE logo</li>\n\n\n\n<li>New 3D-printed yoke</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Packable design</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Made in the USA at Stinner’s Santa Barbara factory</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<figure>\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-ps-left.jpeg\"><img width=\"1280\" height=\"886\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-ps-left.jpeg\" alt=\"Stinner Frameworks Fall:Winter Launch ps left\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-ps-left.jpeg 1280w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-ps-left-297x206.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-ps-left-120x83.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-ps-left-768x532.jpeg 768w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-ps-right.jpeg\"><img width=\"1280\" height=\"854\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-ps-right.jpeg\" alt=\"Stinner Frameworks Fall:Winter Launch ps right\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-ps-right.jpeg 1280w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-ps-right-297x198.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-ps-right-120x80.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-ps-right-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-ps-right-800x533.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-ps-right-720x480.jpeg 720w\" /></a></figure>\n</figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Stinner says that makes it stronger while cutting fabrication time. It’s packable for travel, finished in bead-blasted titanium with a black Stinner x MADE logo, and made in the USA. It’s $109.99, which is cheaper than most of the “stuff I definitely needed” in my shop. We’re fans of the Photo Stick for obvious reasons, but for version 3.0, we’d love to see a way to adjust the length to fit different bikes a little better. </p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Stoic Wheelsets Retail &amp; Details</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>All Stoic wheelsets carry a flatness tolerance of 0.2 mm max, and a roundness 0.3mm max. Tubeless tape and valves included.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3>The Stoic R40 (All-Road)</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Retail: From $1,499 </p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-R40.jpeg\"><img width=\"1280\" height=\"854\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-R40.jpeg\" alt=\"Stinner Frameworks Fall:Winter Launch R40\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-R40.jpeg 1280w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-R40-297x198.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-R40-120x80.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-R40-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-R40-800x533.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-R40-720x480.jpeg 720w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul>\n<li>Fits Gibraltar and Carrizo</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Toray T700/T800 carbon, 700c, hooked and tubeless ready</li>\n\n\n\n<li>25mm internal / 32mm external / 40mm deep, asymmetric with 2.6mm offset</li>\n\n\n\n<li>24h front and rear, rim weight 420g</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Max tire pressure 125 psi, max spoke tension 140 kgf, rider weight limit 120kg (265 lb)</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Hubs: Stoic, made with Bitex (BX106F/R), 12×100/12x142mm thru-axle, Center Lock</li>\n\n\n\n<li>6-pawl freehub, 44 points of engagement</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Freehub options: Shimano HG 11/12spd, SRAM XDR, Campagnolo N3W, Shimano Micro Spline (upgrade kit)</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Sealed cartridge bearings</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pillar PSR Triple Butted spokes, Pillar brass nipples, J-bend</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Hub weights: front ~126g, rear ~230-250g</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Wheelset weight: 1,535g (taped, no valves)</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<figure>\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-r40-right.jpeg\"><img width=\"1280\" height=\"854\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-r40-right.jpeg\" alt=\"Stinner Frameworks Fall:Winter Launch r40 right\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-r40-right.jpeg 1280w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-r40-right-297x198.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-r40-right-120x80.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-r40-right-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-r40-right-800x533.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-r40-right-720x480.jpeg 720w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-r40-left.jpeg\"><img width=\"1280\" height=\"854\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-r40-left.jpeg\" alt=\"Stinner Frameworks Fall:Winter Launch r40 left\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-r40-left.jpeg 1280w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-r40-left-297x198.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-r40-left-120x80.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-r40-left-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-r40-left-800x533.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-r40-left-720x480.jpeg 720w\" /></a></figure>\n</figure>\n\n\n\n<h3>Stoic G29 (Gravel)</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Retail: From $1,499</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-g29.jpeg\"><img width=\"1280\" height=\"854\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-g29.jpeg\" alt=\"Stinner Frameworks Fall:Winter Launch g29\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-g29.jpeg 1280w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-g29-297x198.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-g29-120x80.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-g29-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-g29-800x533.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-g29-720x480.jpeg 720w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul>\n<li>Fits Refugio</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Toray T700/T800 carbon, 29″/700c, hookless (3mm bead wall), tubeless only</li>\n\n\n\n<li>29mm internal / 35mm external / 25mm deep, asymmetric with 2.6mm or 3mm offset</li>\n\n\n\n<li>24h front and rear, rim weight 400g</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Same Stoic/Bitex hubs, 6-pawl freehub, and freehub options as the R40</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pillar PSR Triple Butted spokes, Pillar brass nipples, J-bend</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Wheelset weight: 1,450g (taped, no valves)</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<figure>\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-g29-left.jpeg\"><img width=\"1280\" height=\"946\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-g29-left.jpeg\" alt=\"Stinner Frameworks Fall:Winter Launch g29 left\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-g29-left.jpeg 1280w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-g29-left-297x220.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-g29-left-120x89.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-g29-left-768x568.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-g29-left-1218x900.jpeg 1218w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-g29-right.jpeg\"><img width=\"1280\" height=\"854\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-g29-right.jpeg\" alt=\"Stinner Frameworks Fall:Winter Launch g29 right\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-g29-right.jpeg 1280w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-g29-right-297x198.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-g29-right-120x80.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-g29-right-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-g29-right-800x533.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-g29-right-720x480.jpeg 720w\" /></a></figure>\n</figure>\n\n\n\n<h3>And the Stoic M34 (Mountain/Adventure)</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Retail: From $1,499</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-M34-wheel-e1795027174375.jpeg\"><img width=\"1040\" height=\"777\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-M34-wheel-e1795027174375.jpeg\" alt=\"Stinner Frameworks Fall:Winter Launch M34 wheel\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-M34-wheel-e1795027174375.jpeg 1040w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-M34-wheel-e1795027174375-297x222.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-M34-wheel-e1795027174375-120x90.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-M34-wheel-e1795027174375-768x574.jpeg 768w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul>\n<li>Fits Romero and Tunnel</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Toray T700/T800 carbon, 29″, hookless (3mm bead wall), tubeless only</li>\n\n\n\n<li>34mm internal / 40mm external / 25mm deep, asymmetric with 2.6mm or 3mm offset</li>\n\n\n\n<li>32h front and rear, rim weight 430g (AM) / 480g (DH)</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Hubs: Stoic/Bitex BX212F/R, 15x110mm and 12x148mm Boost thru-axle, steel rear axle, Center Lock</li>\n\n\n\n<li>6-pawl freehub, 54 points of engagement</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Freehub options: SRAM XD/XDR, Shimano Micro Spline 12spd, Shimano HG</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Sealed cartridge bearings</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pillar PSR Triple Butted spokes, Pillar brass nipples, J-bend</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Hub weights: front ~142g, rear ~270g</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<figure>\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-M34-left.jpeg\"><img width=\"794\" height=\"1280\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-M34-left.jpeg\" alt=\"Stinner Frameworks Fall:Winter Launch M34 left\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-M34-left.jpeg 794w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stinner-Frameworks-FallWinter-Launch-M34-left-186x300.jpeg 186w, https:/